#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:3
msgid "Use with pre-commit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:5
msgid ""
"Run a pipx app as a `pre-commit <https://pre-commit.com/>`_ hook. This is "
"useful for apps that work with ``pipx run`` but have no native pre-commit "
"support, when you want the prebuilt wheel from PyPI rather than a source "
"build, or when you need pipx's ``--spec`` and ``--index-url`` flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:11
msgid "Add the hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:13
msgid ""
"Add this to your ``.pre-commit-config.yaml``, using the code linter `yapf "
"<https://github.com/google/yapf/>`_ as the example. Set ``rev`` to the "
"latest pipx release tag from the `releases page <https://github.com/pypa/"
"pipx/releases>`_ (``1.15.0`` shown here):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:17
msgid ""
"- repo: https://github.com/pypa/pipx\n"
"  rev: \"1.15.0\"\n"
"  hooks:\n"
"    - id: pipx\n"
"      alias: yapf\n"
"      name: yapf\n"
"      args: [yapf, -i]\n"
"      types: [python]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:28
msgid ""
"The ``args`` list is passed to ``pipx run``: the first item is the app to "
"run, the rest are its arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:32
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:34
msgid "$ pre-commit run yapf --all-files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/use-with-pre-commit.rst:38
msgid "The hook resolves the app through ``pipx run`` and reports its result."
msgstr ""
